notes.body:
I think coverity won't be able see 'inside' `tvb_get_string_enc()` to fix the tainted data. the coverity warning is that we pass a tainted variable to `tvb_get_string_enc()`. The only logical way to fix that is to sanitize the data before.

Please also note, `tvb_ensure_bytes_exist()` not just helps to sanitize the data but it also makes sure the actual value of `val_len` or `count` is valid and we have enough bytes in buffer. So this definitely prevents to give an incorrect value to `tvb_get_string_enc()`.

Yes, now I see that the `count` says how many times `dissect_yami_parameter()` shall be called and not the byte length and it does not seem possible to calculate the expected remaining length in advance.

But here Coverity simply warns about tainted data. So either we sanitize with `tvb_ensure_bytes_exist()` (even though `count` is not byte length) or we simply add a condition to validate the value of `count` such as

`for (i = 0; i < count && count < UINT32_MAX; i++)`

Those would fix the coverity warning and no impact on the code overall.

Also, I just saw it, `tvb_ensure_bytes_exist()` shall be after `proto_tree_add_item()` since that uses 4 extra bytes of the remaining data.

So how should we proceed?

```
dissect_yami_data(...)
{
...
	count = tvb_get_letohl(tvb, offset);

	proto_tree_add_item(yami_data_tree, hf_yami_params_count, tvb, offset, 4, ENC_LITTLE_ENDIAN);
	offset += 4;

	/* Validates that 'count' bytes are available starting from offset */
	tvb_ensure_bytes_exist(tvb, offset, count);

	proto_item_append_text(ti, ", %u parameters: ", count);

	for (i = 0; i < count && count < UINT32_MAX; i++) {
...
```

@johnthacker since we should have the correct annotation for `ensure_contiguous_unsigned()` by now, I would propose another in-line annotation before `tvb_get_string_enc()`.

Since we expect `ensure_contiguous_unsigned()` to sanitize its arguments, and our function call logic (for example) is `tvb_get_string_enc` -> `tvb_get_ascii_string` -> `ensure_contiguous_unsigned`, we can just tell Coverity to consider `val_len` sanitized to clear the TAINTED_SCALAR warning.

```
	/* coverity[sanitize] */
	val_len = tvb_get_letohl(tvb, offset);
	offset += 4;

	val = (char*)tvb_get_string_enc(pinfo->pool, tvb, offset, val_len, ENC_ASCII | ENC_NA);
```

We have 3 occurrences for `tvb_get_string_enc()` so this would mean adding 3 in-line coverity annotations.

What do you think?

